  "notes": "Selection maximizes the summed classifier score over jet-disjoint candidate sets of size <=2 per event (exact enumeration per event, not sequential greedy), after removing candidates below score_threshold. Threshold and method were chosen via a scan on the validation split: threshold=0.03 with the exact/optimal disjoint-pair objective achieved the maximum attainable validation efficiency (0.756) while cutting roughly 18% of low-confidence noise selections relative to threshold=0, improving purity from 0.32 to 0.39 with no efficiency loss. A purely sequential greedy selection (pick top score, then best remaining disjoint) was also tested and found to underperform the exact pairwise-optimal selection by ~1.5 points of efficiency at every threshold."
